  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Same-Origin Policy: The Wall CORS Opens",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Origin Is A Triple",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Origin = scheme + host + port. All three must match, exactly, byte for byte."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Compared to `https://a.com`",
            "Same?",
            "Differs by"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`http://a.com`",
              "no",
              "scheme"
            ],
            [
              "`https://api.a.com`",
              "no",
              "host"
            ],
            [
              "`https://a.com:8443`",
              "no",
              "port"
            ],
            [
              "`https://a.com/y`",
              "yes",
              "path only"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Path is NOT part of an origin",
            "`/x` and `/y` are same-origin, always",
            "`document.domain` relaxation: removed, dead",
            "Never design a new system around it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Site Is Not Origin"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "Same-site",
                "lines": [
                  "eTLD+1 + scheme",
                  "`a.example.com`",
                  "`b.example.com`",
                  "cookie scope"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "Same-origin",
                "lines": [
                  "scheme+host+port",
                  "strictly equal",
                  "SOP scope",
                  "stricter"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Who Enforces It"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "SOP is a browser rule, not a server rule",
            "`curl`, Postman, server-to-server: unaffected",
            "Browser extensions bypass CORS entirely",
            "So CORS never replaces server-side authz"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Read Blocked, Send Allowed",
          "text": "SOP blocks reading the cross-origin response; it often does not block sending the request. That asymmetry is the root of CSRF."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Backward Compatibility"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`<img>`, `<script>`, `<link rel=stylesheet>` load cross-origin",
            "`<iframe>` embeds, `<form>` posts cross-origin",
            "All free since 1996 — CORS could not break them",
            "So CORS only gates `fetch`/XHR reads"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What CORS Actually Is"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Cross-Origin Resource Sharing: a server opt-in",
            "Server says 'this origin may read my response'",
            "Not authentication, not authorization",
            "Browser is the enforcer — server already ran it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "The `null` Origin",
          "items": [
            "From sandboxed iframes",
            "From `file://` pages",
            "From some redirect chains",
            "Never treat `null` as trusted"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Mental Model",
          "text": "CORS is a read-permission handshake between browser and server, negotiated purely with HTTP headers."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "// preflighted: JSON content-type",
            "fetch(u, {method:'POST',",
            "  headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json'},",
            "  body:'{}'})  // OPTIONS fires first"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Anatomy of a CORS Exchange",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The `Origin` Header",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Browser adds `Origin` automatically on cross-origin fetch/XHR",
            "JS cannot set it, spoof it, or delete it",
            "Sent on simple requests too — server always knows",
            "So the server can decide before it answers"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "JS `fetch`",
              "browser adds `Origin`",
              "server",
              "ACAO check",
              "JS reads or throws"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "`Access-Control-Allow-Origin`"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "ACAO value",
            "Valid?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`*`",
              "yes, no credentials"
            ],
            [
              "`https://a.com`",
              "yes, exact echo"
            ],
            [
              "`https://a.com, https://b.com`",
              "no, lists banned"
            ],
            [
              "`https://*.a.com`",
              "no, no inner wildcard"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const o = req.headers.origin",
            "if (ALLOW.has(o)) {",
            "  res.set('Access-Control-Allow-Origin', o)",
            "  res.set('Vary', 'Origin')  // cache safety",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Request Flavors"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flowchart",
          "spec": {
            "title": "cross-origin fetch",
            "rows": [
              [
                "n0"
              ],
              [
                "b0",
                "b1"
              ],
              [
                "c0_0",
                "c0_1"
              ],
              [
                "c1_0",
                "c1_1"
              ]
            ],
            "nodes": {
              "n0": {
                "text": "cross-origin fetch",
                "shape": "diamond"
              },
              "b0": {
                "text": "simple"
              },
              "b1": {
                "text": "preflighted"
              },
              "c0_0": {
                "text": "fires now"
              },
              "c0_1": {
                "text": "check response"
              },
              "c1_0": {
                "text": "OPTIONS probe"
              },
              "c1_1": {
                "text": "then real request"
              }
            },
            "edges": [
              {
                "from": "n0",
                "to": "b0"
              },
              {
                "from": "n0",
                "to": "b1"
              },
              {
                "from": "b0",
                "to": "c0_0"
              },
              {
                "from": "b0",
                "to": "c0_1"
              },
              {
                "from": "b1",
                "to": "c1_0"
              },
              {
                "from": "b1",
                "to": "c1_1"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "How Failure Looks"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Request executes; response reaches the browser",
            "Browser discards it before JS sees it",
            "JS gets `TypeError: Failed to fetch`",
            "No status, no headers — deliberately opaque"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "'But I Can See It!'",
          "text": "DevTools shows the response body even when JS is blocked. The network tab is not JS. Opacity prevents error detail becoming a side channel."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Anatomy of a CORS Exchange (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Reading Response Headers"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Without opt-in, JS sees only safelisted response headers",
            "`Access-Control-Expose-Headers` widens that set",
            "Common bite: `X-Request-Id` invisible until listed",
            "Same for an echoed `Authorization`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Safelisted Response Headers",
          "items": [
            "`Cache-Control`, `Content-Language`",
            "`Content-Length`, `Content-Type`",
            "`Expires`, `Last-Modified`",
            "`Pragma` — that is the whole list"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Errors Need Headers Too",
          "text": "CORS headers must appear on 4xx/5xx responses. Otherwise the client sees a CORS error instead of your real 500."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "All Conditions, Not Any",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A request is simple only if method, headers, content-type and body shape ALL qualify. One violation forces a preflight."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Dimension",
            "Simple if"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "method",
              "`GET`, `HEAD`, `POST`"
            ],
            [
              "content-type",
              "form-urlencoded, multipart, text/plain"
            ],
            [
              "headers",
              "safelisted only"
            ],
            [
              "body",
              "no `ReadableStream`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`PUT`, `PATCH`, `DELETE` always preflight",
            "`application/json` is the #1 accidental preflight",
            "Any custom header forces the probe",
            "No listener on `XMLHttpRequest.upload`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Safelisted Request Headers"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "The Short List",
          "items": [
            "`Accept`, `Accept-Language`",
            "`Content-Language`",
            "`Content-Type` (safelisted values only)",
            "`Range` (simple range values)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`X-API-Key`, `Authorization`, `X-Requested-With`: not safelisted",
            "Even a safelisted header can exceed byte limits",
            "Over-long values silently force a preflight"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Concrete Calls"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "// simple: no OPTIONS at all",
            "fetch(u, {method:'POST',",
            "  body: new URLSearchParams({a:1})})"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Why This Set Exists"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Simple = shapes an HTML `<form>` could already send",
            "Those shapes were reachable before CORS existed",
            "So no permission probe can be required for them",
            "The safelist is a compatibility fossil, not a design"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Simple Requests: The No-Preflight Path",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "CSRF Is Still Yours",
          "text": "A simple cross-origin POST reaches your handler and runs before any CORS check happens. CORS never stopped the write."
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Can I dodge preflight on a JSON API?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Yes: send `Content-Type: text/plain`, parse manually",
            "Server does `JSON.parse(rawBody)` itself",
            "But you delete the browser's CSRF-ish speed bump",
            "Only do it with real anti-CSRF tokens in place"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "fetch(u,{method:'POST',",
            "  headers:{'Content-Type':'text/plain'},",
            "  body: JSON.stringify(payload)})"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What Preflight Is",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "An automatic `OPTIONS` request the browser sends before the real one, asking permission for the method and headers."
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "OPTIONS probe",
              "server 204",
              "cached?",
              "real PUT",
              "second CORS check"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What The Probe Sends"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "OPTIONS /v1/items HTTP/1.1",
            "Origin: https://app.com",
            "Access-Control-Request-Method: PUT",
            "Access-Control-Request-Headers: content-type,x-api-key"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Requested headers arrive lowercased, comma-separated",
            "Preflight carries no body",
            "It must be answerable without auth"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What The Server Must Answer"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Header",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`Allow-Origin`",
              "who may read"
            ],
            [
              "`Allow-Methods`",
              "`GET, POST, PUT, DELETE`"
            ],
            [
              "`Allow-Headers`",
              "every non-safelisted header"
            ],
            [
              "status",
              "200 or 204, no body"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Allow-Methods` answers the preflight, not per-route policy",
            "`Allow-Headers: *` works only without credentials",
            "Every custom header must be named, or the probe fails"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Preflight: The OPTIONS Handshake",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Classic Breakages"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Auth middleware runs first, returns `401` to OPTIONS",
            "Router has no OPTIONS handler: `404` or `405`",
            "Redirects are never followed on preflight",
            "A `http`→`https` `301` on OPTIONS kills the exchange"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "401 Reads As CORS",
          "text": "The browser reports a CORS error, never an auth error, when OPTIONS returns 401. Look at the OPTIONS status line first, always."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Reading It In DevTools"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Filter the network tab by method OPTIONS",
            "Diff `Access-Control-Request-Headers` against `Allow-Headers`",
            "Compare line by line — one missing name fails all",
            "Preflight fail = real request never sent"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Server Log Tell",
          "items": [
            "Only an `OPTIONS` line appears",
            "No matching `PUT`/`POST` line",
            "That means the probe was rejected",
            "Not a client bug — a config bug"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Two Checks, Not One",
          "text": "The real response must also carry a valid ACAO. Preflight approval alone grants nothing; the second check can still fail."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Preflight costs a full round trip. On a high-latency link it can roughly double perceived API latency."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Credentials Are Opt-In",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mode",
            "Cookies sent?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`same-origin` (default)",
              "only same-origin"
            ],
            [
              "`include`",
              "yes, cross-origin"
            ],
            [
              "`omit`",
              "never"
            ],
            [
              "`xhr.withCredentials = true`",
              "XHR equivalent"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`include` also sends TLS client certs",
            "`include` lets `Set-Cookie` in the response stick",
            "Default mode sends nothing cross-origin"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Both Gates Must Open"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "Client side",
                "lines": [
                  "`credentials:'include'`",
                  "or `withCredentials`",
                  "one alone = no cookie"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "Server side",
                "lines": [
                  "`Allow-Credentials: true`",
                  "exact origin echo",
                  "`Vary: Origin`"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "The Wildcard Ban",
          "text": "With credentials, `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` is rejected outright. The server must echo the exact origin string back."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Credentials: Cookies, Auth, and the Wildcard Ban",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Same ban hits `Allow-Headers: *` and `Allow-Methods: *`",
            "And `Expose-Headers: *` — literal `*`, not a wildcard",
            "Preflight must ALSO return `Allow-Credentials: true`",
            "Missing that header blocks the read even if ACAO is right"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Exact Error"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "The value of the Access-Control-Allow-Origin",
            "header must not be the wildcard '*' when the",
            "request's credentials mode is 'include'"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cache Safety With Echo"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Echoing an origin makes the response origin-dependent",
            "Without `Vary: Origin` a shared cache mixes them up",
            "One tenant then receives another tenant's ACAO",
            "So `Vary: Origin` is mandatory, not optional"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "SameSite Is A Second Gate"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`SameSite=Lax` is the modern default",
            "Lax blocks the cookie on cross-site fetch/XHR",
            "Even with CORS fully, correctly configured",
            "Cross-site needs `SameSite=None; Secure`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Two Independent Gates",
          "text": "CORS and SameSite decide different things and neither implies the other. Third-party cookie deprecation is eroding `None; Secure` too."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Bearer Tokens Sidestep It"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Is `Authorization: Bearer` a CORS credential?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "No — in CORS terms it is a custom header",
            "It forces a preflight and needs `Allow-Headers`",
            "It does NOT need `Allow-Credentials: true`",
            "So it dodges the wildcard trap entirely"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "fetch(u, {headers:",
            "  {Authorization:'Bearer '+t}})",
            "// preflights, but no cookie rules apply"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That is the practical reason bearer tokens are simpler than cookies for cross-origin APIs."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "`Access-Control-Max-Age`",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "HTTP/1.1 204 No Content",
            "Access-Control-Allow-Origin: https://app.com",
            "Access-Control-Allow-Methods: PUT, DELETE",
            "Access-Control-Max-Age: 600  # skip OPTIONS 10min"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Caching Preflights and Vary",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Caches the preflight result, skipping the round trip",
            "Cache key = (origin, URL, method, header set)",
            "A different method or header set re-preflights",
            "`Max-Age: 0` disables it — use while debugging"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Browsers Cap Your Value"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Browser",
            "Effective cap"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Chromium",
              "7200s (2h)"
            ],
            [
              "Firefox",
              "86400s (24h)"
            ],
            [
              "Safari",
              "historically ~600s"
            ],
            [
              "your header",
              "only ever lowered"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Missing OPTIONS In Logs",
          "text": "Preflights appear once per cache window. A silent log does not mean the probe never happened — it may just be cached."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "`Vary: Origin` Is Mandatory"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Required whenever ACAO depends on the request `Origin`",
            "CDNs and reverse proxies key their cache on `Vary`",
            "Without it, one cached ACAO is served to everyone",
            "A static `ACAO: *` needs no `Vary` — origin-independent"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "evil.com asks",
              "CDN caches ACAO evil",
              "app.com asks",
              "serves evil ACAO",
              "app breaks"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Poisoning, Both Ways",
          "items": [
            "Attacker origin cached, app blocked",
            "Or app origin cached, leak widened",
            "Same missing header causes both",
            "`Vary: Origin` fixes both"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Vary On Preflights Too"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Add `Vary: Access-Control-Request-Headers`",
            "And `Vary: Access-Control-Request-Method`",
            "Needed when the answer varies by them",
            "Otherwise one probe's answer serves a different shape"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Reducing Preflight Cost"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Keep endpoints simple-request-shaped where possible",
            "Or raise `Max-Age`, or consolidate custom headers",
            "Preflight cache is per-browser-profile",
            "Hard reload with 'Disable cache' clears it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Cached Config Regression",
          "text": "A cached preflight can mask a server-side CORS regression for hours after a deploy. High Max-Age slows propagation of every fix."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Caching Preflights and Vary (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Measure it: on a 100ms RTT link a preflighted call costs ~200ms before the first byte of real work."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "`fetch` Modes",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mode",
            "Cross-origin result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`cors` (default)",
              "readable if allowed"
            ],
            [
              "`no-cors`",
              "opaque, status 0"
            ],
            [
              "`same-origin`",
              "rejected outright"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`no-cors` is not a bypass — the body stays unreadable",
            "Useful only for fire-and-forget or cache warming",
            "Opaque responses still eat cache storage quota",
            "And they are padded, so at an inflated size"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Redirects Are Hops"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Every hop in the chain must pass CORS",
            "Cross-origin redirect can reset the origin to `null`",
            "`redirect: 'manual'` yields an opaque-redirect response",
            "`redirect: 'error'` fails fast — good for diagnosis"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "await fetch(u, {redirect:'error'})",
            "// throws on any hidden hop",
            "// use to find a sneaky http->https 301"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Neighbours, Not Synonyms"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mechanism",
            "Decides"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "CORS",
              "who may READ your response"
            ],
            [
              "CSP",
              "what your page may LOAD"
            ],
            [
              "CSRF tokens",
              "whether a write is intended"
            ],
            [
              "CORP",
              "who may EMBED your resource"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "CORS does not stop a request from executing",
            "State-changing routes need SameSite + anti-CSRF tokens",
            "JSONP was the pre-CORS `<script>` callback hack",
            "No method control, no header control, runs attacker JS"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "JSONP Is Dead",
          "text": "It executes third-party JS in your page with zero controls. Never revive it, not even for one legacy endpoint."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Isolation Headers"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "CORP values: `same-origin | same-site | cross-origin`",
            "COOP + COEP enable cross-origin isolation",
            "Isolation unlocks `SharedArrayBuffer`, precise timers",
            "`Timing-Allow-Origin` gates Resource Timing detail"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Beyond Basic CORS: Redirects, Modes, and Neighbors",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Under COEP `require-corp`",
          "items": [
            "Every cross-origin subresource must send CORP",
            "Or be fetched with real CORS",
            "A whole new class of load failures",
            "Audit fonts, images, analytics first"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Private Network Access"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Public page calling a local IP triggers PNA",
            "Adds `Access-Control-Request-Private-Network`",
            "Breaks many `localhost` dev setups",
            "Local server must opt in explicitly"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "WebSockets Opt Out",
          "text": "WebSockets do not use CORS at all. The server must read and validate the `Origin` header itself during the handshake."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Pick Your Pattern",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
