          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Express"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "app.use(cors({origin: ALLOWED,",
            "  credentials: true}))   // BEFORE auth",
            "app.options('*', cors())  // if no auto OPTIONS",
            "app.use(auth)"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Nginx"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "nginx",
          "lines": [
            "if ($request_method = OPTIONS) {",
            "  add_header Access-Control-Allow-Origin $o;",
            "  return 204;",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`add_header` is NOT inherited into a block with its own",
            "Repeat every CORS header per block",
            "Use `always` so headers survive error responses"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Spring & Django"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`@CrossOrigin(origins=\"https://app.com\", allowCredentials=\"true\")`",
            "Or a global `CorsConfigurationSource` bean",
            "Spring Security needs `http.cors()` or OPTIONS is rejected",
            "Django: `django-cors-headers` + `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Never In Production",
          "text": "`CORS_ALLOW_ALL_ORIGINS = True` combined with credentials. It is the reflect-any-origin bug shipped as a config flag."
